000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. MERGE2.
000300* MERGE of two files already in order, USING and GIVING: two
000400* keys, one descending on a DISPLAY number, one ascending on
000500* characters. Records equal on every key come out in the order of
000600* the files in USING, and within a file in the order they were
000700* read: the 1974 standard's rule for MERGE. IBM ANS COBOL has no
000800* MERGE and the system sort merges only when JCL starts it, so
000900* the expected output is the standard's rule, worked by hand.
001000 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
001100 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001200 FILE-CONTROL.
001300     SELECT IN1-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-INFILE1.
001400     SELECT IN2-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-INFILE2.
001500     SELECT OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-OUTFILE.
001600     SELECT MERGE-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-SORTWK01.
001700 DATA DIVISION.
001800 FILE SECTION.
001900 FD  IN1-FILE LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
002000 01  IN1-REC PIC X(80).
002100 FD  IN2-FILE LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
002200 01  IN2-REC PIC X(80).
002300 FD  OUT-FILE LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
002400 01  OUT-REC PIC X(80).
002500 SD  MERGE-FILE.
002600 01  M-REC.
002700     05  M-NAME   PIC X(10).
002800     05  M-DEPT   PIC 99.
002900     05  M-REST   PIC X(68).
003000 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
003100 01  EOF PIC X VALUE 'N'.
003200 01  SR  PIC S9(4).
003300 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
003400 MAIN-PARA.
003500     MERGE MERGE-FILE DESCENDING KEY M-DEPT ASCENDING KEY M-NAME
003600         USING IN1-FILE IN2-FILE GIVING OUT-FILE.
003700     MOVE SORT-RETURN TO SR.
003800     DISPLAY 'SORT-RETURN ' SR.
003900     OPEN INPUT OUT-FILE.
004000     READ OUT-FILE AT END MOVE 'Y' TO EOF.
004100     PERFORM SHOW-ONE UNTIL EOF = 'Y'.
004200     CLOSE OUT-FILE.
004300     DISPLAY 'END OF OUT-FILE'.
004400     STOP RUN.
004500 SHOW-ONE.
004600     DISPLAY OUT-REC.
004700     READ OUT-FILE AT END MOVE 'Y' TO EOF.
